Creative Catalyst: its founding artists were botanists who sonified the electrical signals of rainforest plants.

It sounds like a hallucinatory garden party held inside a cloud of pressurized chlorophyll, where lightning-fast boom-bap vocal cadences duel with hyper-complex, shifting time signatures of distorted jazz-rock fusion. The music swims in vast, misty atmospheric pads that smell faintly of ozone and crushed ferns, anchored relentlessly by a virtuosic, heavy-gutted Bass Guitar playing hyper-slapped, sub-aquatic funk lines translated directly from the bio-electric voltage fluctuations of giant monstera leaves.

Genre DNA
- Tempo & Pulse: 94 to 108 BPM; a lurching, polyrhythmic swing that combines the swinging swagger of 1980s park jams with the frantic, asymmetrical meters of 1970s jazz-fusion.
- Harmonic Palette: Lydian dominant and altered pentatonic scales, drenched in floating major-seventh voicings that feel weightless, yet continuously grounded by aggressive, earth-shaking low-end bass frequencies.
- Production Signatures: Gated tape-delay vocals fed through a hardware rig hooked up to live damp moss; micro-tonal pitch-bending achieved via humidity-sensor CV triggers; sprawling, airy stereo imaging that makes the mix sound like it is breathing in and out.
- Dynamics: The music ebbs and flows like a tropical microclimate, violently erupting from wispy, cloud-like ambient silence into towering, cacophonous walls of slap-bass fury and rapid-fire rhyming, before dissolving back into dew.

